  "borough": "London Borough of Sutton",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed rear dormer extension, by virtue of its excessive width, box-like design, and flat-roofed appearance, would be a bulky and unsympathetic addition that fails to respect the scale and character of the original dwelling. The proposal represents an overdevelopment of the roof slope, appearing top-heavy and visually intrusive, contrary to Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018) and the 'Design of Residential Extensions' SPD4.",
    "The proposed development, specifically the inclusion of the rear dormer, would result in an adverse impact on the living conditions of the occupiers of April Dew. Due to the increased scale and elevated position of the habitable space, the proposal would result in an overbearing impact and a loss of privacy through actual and perceived overlooking of the neighbouring private amenity space. This is contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018) and the 'Design of Residential Extensions' SPD4."
  ],
